Alembic migration foundation
============================

The shared metadata is db.base.Base.metadata. The environment explicitly
imports models.customer to register the Customer model. Register future ORM
modules explicitly before using their tables in migration comparisons.

Offline mode uses a credential-free postgresql+psycopg dialect URL. It does
not import db.database, load .env, or connect to a database. Online mode
imports the application's shared engine only inside run_migrations_online.
Do not place credentials in alembic.ini or add connection URL/parameter logs.

Safe offline checks from the project root (PowerShell):
    .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -B -m alembic history
    .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -B -m alembic heads
    .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -B -m alembic upgrade head --sql

Verified offline on 2026-10-31 using the project virtual environment:
history and heads exited successfully with no revisions. Offline upgrade
exited successfully and emitted only BEGIN and COMMIT, with no table DDL.
An in-process environment check confirmed that target_metadata is the shared
Base.metadata and contains customers; db.database and dotenv were not imported.
Importing models does not generate migration operations.

No revisions are included in this foundation. Revision creation and online
database operations require a separately approved development task. Offline
checks do not validate database connectivity, permissions, existing tables,
applied revisions, or actual constraint behavior.
